 {
  "id": "cook.provenance.origin-query",
  "status": "survived",
  "class": "shadowed by an earlier check",
  "analysis": "The mutant deletes `not url.query` in `registry_origin` (archive.py:44). `urlsplit` yields a non-empty query only from text after a `?`, and archive.py:39 refuses every value that contains `?` before the URL is parsed. So when the query test runs, the query is empty. test/mutants/shadowed_repository.py found no origin that reaches the test with a query among 200,000 seeded values. The vector `archive.registry-origin.empty-query` shows that even a bare trailing `?` is refused by the character test."
 },
