 {
  "id": "archive.L140.4",
  "status": "crash-only",
  "class": "only a runtime error distinguishes it, in both engines",
  "analysis": "The mutant deletes `need(isinstance(manifest, dict), ...)` in `archive_manifest` (archive.py:140). The next statement calls `manifest.get`, which exists only on a mapping, so for every other JSON value (list, string, number, null) the oracle mutant raises AttributeError and the TS mutant raises the modelled AttributeError: a refusal becomes a runtime error and nothing else changes. No function in the five ported modules catches that class around `archive_manifest`; the callers that do (`cook.main`, the deployment boundary) are not ported, and there the public code would differ. Vector: `archive.manifest.manifest.list`. This is the phase-1 crash-only category; it is not counted as killed."
